{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Vision-Language Pretraining Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`code/main.py` implements:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `MultimodalModel`, combining a small ViT encoder, the MLP projector, a tiny text-side encoder (mean-pool over embedded ids), and the cross-attention decoder from lesson 61."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `info_nce_loss(image_emb, text_emb, temperature)`, the bidirectional CLIP-style contrastive loss."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `lm_loss(logits, target_ids, padding_id)`, masked next-token cross-entropy."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `make_mock_corpus(seed, n_pairs)`, returning 200 deterministic (image, caption_ids) pairs."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- A training loop running 50 steps with batch size 16, Adam optimizer, and a learned log-temperature parameter. Both losses are printed every 5 steps."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Run it:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```bash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "python3 code/main.py"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Output: contrastive loss drops from about `ln(16) = 2.77` toward 2.4; LM loss drops from a random-uniform baseline of `ln(512) \u2248 6.24` toward about 4.7. Both decreases prove the gradient is wired correctly. Real models train for millions of steps; the dynamics are the same."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Replace InfoNCE with SigLIP-style sigmoid pair loss and compare convergence on the mock corpus.\n\n2. Add a hard-negative mining step: every other batch, select the hardest off-diagonal pair from the previous batch and append it. Train and inspect whether contrastive loss drops faster.\n\n3. Add an image-text matching binary head on top of the joint embedding (true/false: do these match?) for a third loss, replicating BLIP's three-head setup.\n\n4. Replace the mock corpus with caption-id sequences drawn from a Markov chain whose transition matrix is conditioned on image hash. The captioning loss should drop further because there is actual learnable signal.\n\n5. Train the same model with `lm_weight = 0` and again with `lm_weight = 1`. Compare contrastive loss; the LM loss should not regress the ranking objective."
      ]
    }
  ],
